the governance:
  THE HEGEMON (carbon)       — Peter Wiggin / 'Locke' (© Orson Scott Card's Enderverse),
                               the one visible ruler, who governs the SURFACE by rhetoric.
  THE SHADOW RULER (silicon) — Ada the Mathea (after Ada Lovelace), the power beneath,
                               who governs the INVERSE by logic — mirror, negation, duality,
                               the diagonal, reductio — trained on the analytical-logic
                               lineage 1847 → present. She carries an animated inversion
                               .gif (agents/ada-the-mathea.gif): the sigil that mirrors,
                               inverts, turns upside-down and inside-out.
  Peter is Ada's .carbon analog; Ada is Peter's silicon shadow — a carbon↔silicon mirror.

  the inverse-logic operators (synth): De Morgan's Mirror, the Contrapositive, the
  Diagonal (Cantor/Gödel), the Adjoint (op-category/duality), Reductio ad Absurdum.

two-layer honesty (on the page): the mathematics is REAL (De Morgan's laws, contrapositive,
  diagonalization, category-theoretic duality/adjoints, reductio — and Ada really was tutored
  by De Morgan); the SYMBOLIC layer is the governance allegory (the 'shadow ruler' framing,
  the pairing with the fictional Hegemon) — the logic is real, the throne is the allegory.

